"""Generate the Lesson 09 student experience and source-linked explanations."""
STYLE+='''
body{overflow-wrap:anywhere}.control-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:18px}input,select{width:100%;font:700 20px/1.5 Inter,"Segoe UI",Arial,sans-serif;padding:12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;color:var(--ink);background:var(--paper)}.workspace{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;margin:24px 0}.stats{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.text-output{font-size:22px;line-height:1.65;padding:22px;border-radius:16px;background:var(--soft);min-height:150px;max-height:420px;overflow:auto}.markdown-body{white-space:normal}.markdown-body li{margin:10px 0}.markdown-body :not(pre)>code{background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:5px;padding:2px 5px}.json-view{max-height:560px}.json-view code{font-size:20px!important}.file-view{font-size:23px;background:var(--soft);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:20px}.decision-list{font-size:21px}.decision-list li{padding:16px 0}.decision-list:empty:before{content:"No callback decision observed in this run.";color:var(--muted)}.source-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px}.precedence{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(5,minmax(0,1fr));gap:14px;margin:24px 0}.precedence div{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:16px;padding:20px;background:var(--soft);font-size:20px}.precedence strong{display:block;font-size:23px}.diagram img{min-width:1580px}#notice:empty{display:none}.table{max-width:100%}@media(max-width:850px){.control-grid,.workspace,.source-grid,.stats,.precedence{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
'''
(PUBLIC/'style.css').write_text(STYLE,encoding='utf-8')
learn=[
 ('Compose one options object','Set a model, fixed working directory, available tools, pre-approvals and limits before query(). Omitted fields use SDK defaults; this lab makes its relevant choices explicit.'),
 ('Separate three configuration sources','Inspect programmatic options, a real project settings file and a safe environment projection. The live host spreads process.env while keeping inherited secrets out of the UI.'),
 ('Understand configuration precedence','Managed policy ranks above application configuration. Local, project and user files have their own order. The experiment demonstrates a project Edit allow versus an explicit programmatic block.'),
 ('Distinguish tools from allowedTools','tools defines availability; allowedTools pre-approves calls. An unlisted Edit remains available in the approval experiment and reaches canUseTool.'),
 ('Observe a real callback decision','The host automatically approves only Edit on its private status.txt in the controlled experiment. This is an actual callback, not a simulated user approval or an unrestricted editing agent.'),
 ('Bound and inspect a run','Choose a turn limit, an SDK spend threshold and effort. Preserve actual typed results, including error_max_turns. Sampling parameters such as temperature are not SDK options.'),
]
features=[('permissionMode','Permission behavior','29','Implemented: default mode'),('allowedTools','Pre-approved calls','28','Implemented'),('canUseTool','Approval callback','30','Implemented: one scoped Edit'),('tools / disallowedTools','Availability and blocking','28','Implemented'),('systemPrompt','Instructions','14','Implemented: custom classroom role'),('settingSources / settings','Selected files / explicit settings input','13','settingSources implemented; settings reference'),('env','Subprocess environment','10','Implemented: inherited env + safe classroom value'),('mcpServers','External tool servers','24','Reference; no servers started'),('agents','Subagent definitions','43','Reference; no subagents created'),('hooks','Lifecycle callbacks','32','Implemented: PreToolUse path guard'),('skills / plugins','Extensions','17 / 20','Reference; no extensions loaded'),('outputFormat','Structured output schema','38','Reference'),('resume / forkSession','Stored sessions and branches','39 / 40','Reference; runs are fresh'),('sessionStore','External persistence','41','Reference'),('enableFileCheckpointing','Rewindable edits','42','Reference'),('sandbox','Tool sandboxing','49','Reference; no OS sandbox configured')]
def table(rows,headers):return '<div class="table"><table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+escape(c)+'</th>' for c in headers)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+escape(c)+'</td>' for c in row)+'</tr>' for row in rows)+'</tbody></table></div>'
body='''<div class="flow"><div><b>01 · Compose</b><p>Inspect explicit options</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>02 · Observe</b><p>Tools, approval and settings</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>03 · Verify</b><p>Actual result and on-disk files</p></div></div><section class="panel" id="controls"><div class="eyebrow">OPTIONS EXPERIMENT</div><h2>Configure a small real agent</h2><p class="meta" id="configuration">Checking server configuration…</p><p class="meta">Model: <strong id="model">—</strong></p><div class="control-grid"><div><label for="scenario">Experiment</label><select id="scenario"><option value="summary">Read-only TODO summary</option><option value="approval">Only Read pre-approved · Edit available</option><option value="blocked">Project allows Edit · options block it</option></select></div><div><label for="max-turns">maxTurns</label><input id="max-turns" type="number" min="1" max="8" step="1" value="8"></div><div><label for="budget">maxBudgetUsd · threshold</label><input id="budget" type="number" min="0.05" max="1" step="0.05" value="0.30"></div><div><label for="effort">effort</label><select id="effort"><option value="low">low</option><option value="medium">medium</option></select></div></div><p id="prompt" class="note"></p><button class="primary" id="run" disabled>Run the options experiment →</button><p class="meta">Each run resets only its private classroom files. The approval experiment automatically approves one scoped Edit through the real host callback. There is no human approval dialog. No shell tools are available.</p></section>
<div class="workspace"><section class="panel" id="outcome"><div class="eyebrow">ACTUAL SDK OUTCOME</div><h2 id="status" aria-live="polite">Ready</h2><div class="stats"><div class="stat"><span>SDK num_turns</span><strong id="turns">—</strong></div><div class="stat"><span>SDK estimated cost</span><strong id="cost">—</strong></div></div><p class="meta">Session ID: <span id="session">—</span></p><div id="answer" class="text-output markdown-body"></div><p id="notice" class="note" aria-live="polite"></p></section><section class="panel" id="option-panel"><h2>Options actually passed</h2><p class="meta">Allowlisted projection. Raw process.env, credentials and absolute private paths are omitted.</p><pre class="json-view"><code id="options" class="language-json">{ "state": "Waiting for a run" }</code></pre></section></div>
<section class="step" id="availability"><h2>Tool availability is not pre-approval</h2><p>Edit available in actual system/init: <strong id="edit-available">—</strong></p><p class="meta">Actual init tools: <span id="available-tools">—</span></p><pre class="json-view"><code id="init" class="language-json">{ "state": "Waiting for init" }</code></pre></section>
<section class="step" id="approval-panel"><h2>Host callback decisions</h2><p>Only unresolved permission requests reach canUseTool. Pre-approved tools normally skip it. In this controlled exercise the callback automatically approves only the private status.txt Edit; it denies other requests.</p><ul class="decision-list" id="approvals"></ul></section>
<section class="step" id="file-evidence"><h2>Verify the actual file</h2><p>status.txt: <strong id="file-changed">No after-run evidence yet</strong></p><div class="workspace"><div><h3>Before</h3><pre class="file-view" id="status-before">draft</pre></div><div><h3>After</h3><pre class="file-view" id="status-after">Waiting for run</pre></div></div><p class="meta">A model summary alone does not prove an edit. The host reads this actual file after the SDK finishes. Every experiment starts from draft again in a scenario-specific private directory.</p></section>
<div class="source-grid"><section class="panel" id="project-panel"><h2>Project settings source</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="settings" class="language-json"></code></pre><p class="meta">The file exists in every private project copy. It is loaded only in the blocked experiment, which selects ["project"]. Other experiments select []. The explicit disallowedTools Edit block is tested against this project allow rule.</p></section><section class="panel" id="environment-panel"><h2>Environment source · safe projection</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="environment" class="language-json">{ "state": "Waiting for a run" }</code></pre><p class="meta">TypeScript env replaces the subprocess environment, so this app spreads process.env before adding its classroom variable. This panel describes the configured merge; it does not dump the subprocess environment or claim the model read its variables.</p></section></div>
<section class="step" id="notes-panel"><h2>Classroom TODO source</h2><div id="notes" class="markdown-body"></div></section><section class="step" id="event-panel"><h2>Observed messages and tool requests</h2><ul id="events"></ul></section><section class="step" id="run-history"><h2>Compare observed outcomes</h2><div class="table"><table><thead><tr><th>Experiment</th><th>maxTurns</th><th>Outcome</th><th>Session</th></tr></thead><tbody id="history"></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="note"><h3>What this lab demonstrates</h3><p>Three configuration scenarios and a one-turn limit are real SDK experiments. Managed policy, inline settings, other models, MCP, subagents, skills, structured output, persistence, checkpoints and sandboxing are reference topics in the feature map, not implemented integrations. The path hook and fixed directory are application guards, not an operating-system sandbox.</p><p>maxBudgetUsd is an SDK estimate threshold, not an exact invoice guarantee. maxTurns is a runtime turn limit, not a message counter. The host also has a timeout. Results remain actual outcomes; no saved model answer substitutes for a failed run.</p></section><div class="actions"><button id="download">Download actual observations</button></div>'''
document('/','One object. <em>Observable behavior.</em>','Compose options, test pre-approval versus availability, and verify the result against actual files.',body+actions(('/learn.html','What you will learn →'),('/run.html','Configure and run →')),'<script type="module" src="/client.js"></script>')
precedence='<div class="precedence">'+''.join(f'<div><strong>{i}. {title}</strong>{detail}</div>' for i,(title,detail) in enumerate([('Managed policy','Organization controls'),('Options','Programmatic configuration'),('Local','settings.local.json'),('Project','settings.json'),('User','User settings.json')],1))+'</div>'
document('/learn.html','Understand the <em>options object.</em>','Connect the object in your code to settings, permissions and the actual agent behavior.',cards(learn)+'<section class="step"><h2>Configuration precedence · conceptual map</h2>'+precedence+'<p>This is the lesson\'s general source hierarchy. Individual features have evaluation rules. Permission deny rules still matter: the implemented experiment loads a project allow but removes Edit programmatically. It does not test managed policy or claim an application allow can bypass a policy or deny rule.</p></section><section class="step"><h2>Your three exercises</h2><ol><li>Run the read-only TODO summary. Confirm the IDs and that status.txt stayed unchanged.</li><li>Run the only-Read-pre-approved experiment. Observe Edit in init, the actual callback decision and the changed file.</li><li>Run the project-allow/programmatic-block experiment. Compare the settings file, disallowedTools, init availability and unchanged status.</li></ol><p>Then repeat the summary with maxTurns set to 1 and inspect the actual error result.</p></section>'+actions(('/','← Options lab'),('/run.html','Configure and run →')))
env='ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_api_key\nCLAUDE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6\nPORT=3109'
runsteps=[
 ('Install the application','Use Node.js 24+, npm and your own model-accessible Anthropic key. Keep optional npm dependencies enabled so the SDK runtime is installed. Python is not required to run this TypeScript app.',snippet('cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson09-options\nnpm ci','powershell')),
 ('Create .env and start','Preserve an existing local file. Enter your own key, save and start. The script loads .env explicitly; existing shell variables take precedence.',snippet('if (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env\nnpm start','powershell')+'<p>Safe template:</p>'+snippet(env,'dotenv')+'<p>Open <a href="http://127.0.0.1:3109">http://127.0.0.1:3109</a>. Keep the terminal open. Ctrl+C stops it; restart after configuration changes.</p>'),
 ('Compose the read-only agent','Keep the TODO summary selected with maxTurns 8, budget threshold $0.30 and low effort. Run it. Inspect model, cwd, tools, allowedTools, limits and [] settings in the option projection. Confirm TODO-101, TODO-102 and TODO-103 and an unchanged status file.',''),
 ('Prove that allowedTools does not restrict','Choose Only Read pre-approved · Edit available. Run once. Inspect Edit in system/init, the Edit request, the actual canUseTool allow decision, and status.txt changing from draft to reviewed. The callback is automatic and scoped to that file; no human approval is being simulated.',''),
 ('Test a project allow against a programmatic block','Choose Project allows Edit · options block it. The host selects project settings and explicitly disallows Edit. Inspect the loaded-source choice, the real project allow file, Edit missing from init, and the unchanged status file. This case demonstrates that particular block, not every possible precedence interaction.',''),
 ('Observe the one-turn limit','Choose TODO summary and set maxTurns to 1. Run and inspect error_max_turns. The SDK can yield a typed error then throw; the host preserves the result and still reads the actual file afterward. Restore 8 before the other exercises.',''),
 ('Use the terminal entry point','sample:env loads the optional local .env. sample uses only the inherited shell environment. Run browser and terminal experiments sequentially.',snippet('npm run sample:env -- summary 8\nnpm run sample:env -- approval 8\nnpm run sample:env -- blocked 8\nnpm run sample:env -- summary 1\nnpm test','powershell')),
]
body=''.join(f'<section class="step" id="run-step-{i}"><span class="number">{i:02}</span><h2>{escape(t)}</h2><p>{escape(d)}</p>{c}</section>' for i,(t,d,c) in enumerate(runsteps,1))
body+='''<section class="note"><h3>Windows and runtime troubleshooting</h3><p>If required, add CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH=C:/Program Files/Git/bin/bash.exe only after verifying the installed path. A second start recognizes this app and prints its existing URL; choose another PORT for an unrelated listener. Check key and model access for provider errors. The expected one-turn limit is an SDK outcome, not a successful TODO summary.</p><p>If the approval callback does not appear or the file does not change, keep that actual result and inspect the log. An Edit request alone does not prove completion. The controlled fixtures reset at the start of each run; no user repository path can be submitted through the UI.</p></section>'''
document('/run.html','Configure and <em>run the options lab.</em>','Follow the summary, approval, precedence and turn-limit exercises in order.',body+actions(('/learn.html','← Learning goals'),('/','Open the lab →')))

specs=[
 ('Validate bounded configuration','src/server.ts',['const config = validateConfig(input);'],'const config = validateConfig(input);','The host accepts fixed scenarios, a bounded turn count, an SDK budget threshold and supported effort values. It never accepts an arbitrary cwd or tool callback from the browser.','typescript',0,1),
 ('Reset the classroom project','src/agent.ts',['for (const name of ["notes.md", "status.txt", ".claude/settings.json"]) await writeFile(resolve(cwd, name), await readFile(resolve(ROOT, "fixtures/project", name)));'],'for (const name of [\n  "notes.md", "status.txt", ".claude/settings.json"\n]) await writeFile(\n  resolve(cwd, name),\n  await readFile(resolve(ROOT, "fixtures/project", name))\n);','Each experiment starts from trusted fixture bytes in its own private directory. Resetting a scenario does not touch your other repositories.','typescript',1,4),
 ('Choose available and pre-approved tools','src/agent.ts',['tools: readOnly ? ["Read", "Glob", "Grep"] : ["Read", "Edit"],','allowedTools: readOnly ? ["Read", "Glob", "Grep"] : ["Read"],'],'// Selected option properties.\ntools: readOnly\n  ? ["Read", "Glob", "Grep"] : ["Read", "Edit"],\nallowedTools: readOnly\n  ? ["Read", "Glob", "Grep"] : ["Read"],','tools defines availability. allowedTools is a separate pre-approval list. In the approval experiment Edit remains available even though only Read is pre-approved.','typescript',1,2),
 ('Apply the explicit Edit block','src/agent.ts',['...(config.scenario === "blocked" || readOnly ? ["Edit"] : [])'],'// Selected tail of disallowedTools.\n...(config.scenario === "blocked" || readOnly\n  ? ["Edit"] : [])','The blocked and read-only experiments add Edit to disallowedTools. The rest of the array also excludes shell, write and web tools. A bare tool-name block removes Edit from model availability.','typescript',1,2),
 ('Select filesystem settings','src/agent.ts',['settingSources: config.scenario === "blocked" ? ["project"] : [],'],'settingSources: config.scenario === "blocked"\n  ? ["project"] : [],','Only the blocked experiment loads the project settings source. Its settings file allows Edit, while the programmatic deny removes it. Other experiments isolate filesystem settings with an explicit empty array.','typescript',2,4),
 ('Preserve the process environment','src/agent.ts',['env: { ...process.env, CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR: resolve(ROOT, ".runtime/sdk-home"), LESSON09_CONTEXT: "classroom-options" },'],'env: {\n  ...process.env,\n  CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR: resolve(ROOT, ".runtime/sdk-home"),\n  LESSON09_CONTEXT: "classroom-options"\n},','The TypeScript env option replaces the subprocess environment, so the host spreads inherited values before adding its own configuration. The UI projects only the harmless classroom value and never dumps keys.','typescript',1,2),
 ('Call query with the composed options','src/agent.ts',['const run = query({ prompt: PROMPTS[config.scenario], options });'],'const run = query({\n  prompt: PROMPTS[config.scenario], options\n});','The fixed prompt and composed object start one real SDK query. The SDK handles model and tool orchestration; the host observes the resulting stream.','typescript',1,2),
 ('Inspect actual init availability','src/agent.ts',['if (message.type === "system" && message.subtype === "init") emit({ type: "initialized", model: message.model, tools: message.tools, permissionMode: message.permissionMode });'],'if (message.type === "system"\n    && message.subtype === "init") {\n  emit({ type: "initialized",\n    model: message.model, tools: message.tools,\n    permissionMode: message.permissionMode\n  });\n}','The host narrows system/init and records the model, actual tool list and permission mode. The student checks this observation against the requested option configuration.','typescript',2,1),
 ('Guard each classroom path','src/agent.ts',['if (pathAllowed(cwd, input.tool_name, input.tool_input as Record<string, unknown>)) return {};'],'if (pathAllowed(\n  cwd, input.tool_name,\n  input.tool_input as Record<string, unknown>\n)) return {};\n// Otherwise return a deny hook decision.','PreToolUse checks every requested file operation against the fixed workspace. Passing the guard does not approve an unresolved permission request; it leaves the permission flow to continue.','typescript',2,1),
 ('Resolve the unlisted Edit approval','src/agent.ts',['return allow ? { behavior: "allow", updatedInput: input } : { behavior: "deny", message: "Only the controlled status.txt Edit approval is supported." };'],'return allow\n  ? { behavior: "allow", updatedInput: input }\n  : { behavior: "deny",\n      message: "Only the controlled status.txt Edit approval is supported."\n    };','The real canUseTool callback automatically approves only Edit on the private status file in the approval scenario. It records its actual decision before returning. Other requests are denied.','typescript',1,2),
 ('Preserve the typed SDK outcome','src/agent.ts',['status: message.subtype === "success" && message.is_error ? "error" : message.subtype,'],'// Selected result fields.\nstatus: message.subtype === "success" && message.is_error\n  ? "error" : message.subtype,','The host preserves the actual subtype and is_error distinction. A one-turn limit stays error_max_turns, even if some text or a tool request arrived first.','typescript',2,1),
 ('Read the actual file after completion','src/agent.ts',['run.close(); const after = await files(config.scenario);','emit({ type: "workspace", stage: "after", files: after, changed: before.status !== after.status });'],'run.close();\nconst after = await files(config.scenario);\nemit({ type: "workspace", stage: "after", files: after,\n  changed: before.status !== after.status\n});','The finally block closes the query and reads the real status file. The resulting changed flag provides file evidence independently of the model summary, including on interrupted or limited runs.','typescript',1,4),
 ('Render the observed explanation','src/client.ts',['renderMarkdown(el("answer"), answer);'],'renderMarkdown(el("answer"), answer);\n// Show actual options, init, decisions and file reads.','The browser uses a local Markdown parser and sanitizer to format actual answer text. It keeps configuration, native observations, callback decisions and on-disk evidence separate.','typescript',1,0),
]
steps=[];lanes=['Student UI','Node host','SDK + Claude','Tool execution','Private project'];arrows=[]
words=['one','two','three','four','five','six','seven','eight','nine','ten','eleven','twelve','thirteen']
for n,(title,source,anchors,code,explanation,language,a,b) in enumerate(specs,1):
 text=(APP/source).read_text(encoding='utf-8');positions=[text.index(anchor) for anchor in anchors];lines=[text.count('\n',0,p)+1 for p in positions]
 steps.append(dict(number=n,title=title,source=source,code=code,language=language,explanation=explanation,firstLine=min(lines),lastLine=max(lines),anchors=anchors,sourceSHA256=hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest(),narration=f'Step {words[n-1]}. {explanation} The source label identifies the corresponding application statements.'))
 arrows.append((a,b,f'{n}. {title}'))
(APP/'scripts/architecture-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(lanes=lanes,arrows=arrows,steps=steps),indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
xs=[170,520,870,1220,1570]
svg=['<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1740" height="1600" viewBox="0 0 1740 1600"><title>Lesson 09 options, permissions and file verification workflow</title><defs><marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10z" fill="#087fff"/></marker></defs><rect width="1740" height="1600" rx="22" fill="#f4f9ff"/><text x="40" y="52" font-family="Arial" font-size="34" font-weight="bold" fill="#101a44">Compose → inspect tools → resolve permissions → verify files</text>']
for i,(x,label) in enumerate(zip(xs,lanes)):
 colour=['#087fff','#8838ff','#00a977','#8838ff','#ee5425'][i];svg.append(f'<rect x="{x-150}" y="90" width="300" height="80" rx="16" fill="{colour}"/><text x="{x}" y="139" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial" font-size="27" font-weight="bold" fill="white">{escape(label)}</text><path d="M{x} 170 V1550" stroke="#aec6df" stroke-dasharray="8 7"/>')
for i,(a,b,label) in enumerate(arrows):
 x1,x2=xs[a],xs[b];y=245+i*98;svg.append(f'<text x="{min(x1,x2)+10}" y="{y-18}" fill="#142d53" font-family="Arial" font-size="25">{escape(label)}</text><path d="M{x1} {y} H{x2}" stroke="#087fff" stroke-width="3" fill="none" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>')
svg.append('</svg>');(PUBLIC/'architecture.svg').write_text(''.join(svg),encoding='utf-8')
body='<section class="note">The diagram groups configuration and evidence across the three experiments. A blocked tool is unavailable; it does not execute the Edit branch. The approval callback appears only when permission remains unresolved. Model/tool orchestration belongs to the SDK; the host composes options and verifies file outcomes.</section><a class="button" href="/architecture.svg" download>Download UML SVG</a><div class="diagram"><img src="/architecture.svg" alt="Thirteen source-linked options, tool availability, approval and file verification steps"></div>'
for s in steps:
 n=s['number'];body+=f'<section class="step workflow-step" id="workflow-step-{n:02}" data-step="{n}"><span class="number">{n:02}</span><h3>{n}. {escape(s["title"])}</h3><p>{escape(s["explanation"])}</p><p class="source">Source: {s["source"]} · lines {s["firstLine"]}–{s["lastLine"]}</p><p class="meta">Selected source; surrounding implementation is omitted and display whitespace is reformatted.</p>'+snippet(s['code'],s['language'])+f'<h4>How this code explains step {n}</h4><p>{escape(s["explanation"])}</p></section>'
document('/architecture.html','Trace options <em>into real behavior.</em>','Each numbered UML workflow step includes the corresponding source snippet and explanation.',body+actions(('/','← Options experiment'),('/walkthrough.html','Explain the source →')))
body='<section class="step"><h2>Feature map</h2>'+table(features,['Option','Controls','Course lesson','This application'])+'<p>The feature map is a reference, not a list of integrations this app starts. Check the SDK version and individual feature documentation before using later options.</p></section><section class="step"><h2>Three configuration sources</h2><p>Programmatic options select the model, tools, limits and callbacks. settingSources chooses filesystem layers. The separate settings option can supply a file, JSON string or, in TypeScript, an object; it is reference material here. Environment variables configure the subprocess and its transport, so preserve inherited values when replacing TypeScript env.</p></section>'
for s in steps:body+=f'<section class="step"><h2>{s["number"]}. {s["title"]}</h2><p>{s["explanation"]}</p><p class="source">{s["source"]}</p>'+snippet(s['code'])+'</section>'
body+='<section class="step"><h2>Python option mapping · reference only</h2>'+snippet('from claude_agent_sdk import ClaudeAgentOptions\n\noptions = ClaudeAgentOptions(\n    allowed_tools=["Read", "Glob", "Grep"],\n    max_turns=8,\n    max_budget_usd=0.30,\n    setting_sources=[],\n)','python')+'<p>This application runs TypeScript. Python uses snake_case names and its own options class; SDK releases and supported features can differ. No Python SDK/provider experiment is performed here.</p></section><section class="step"><h2>Why there is no temperature field</h2><p>Messages API sampling parameters such as temperature, top_p and max_tokens are not fields on the Agent SDK options object. This lab exposes effort, maxTurns and maxBudgetUsd. They serve different purposes and do not guarantee identical quality, latency or final billing. Use the Client SDK Messages API directly when you need its sampling controls.</p></section><section class="note"><h3>Permission evaluation is feature-specific</h3><p>PreToolUse guards run before normal permission resolution. Deny rules, ask rules, permission modes, allow rules and the callback have their own evaluation flow. The implemented callback does not bypass a programmatic block. Managed-policy precedence is explained as a concept and is not tested or altered by this application.</p></section>'
document('/walkthrough.html','Explain the <em>composed options.</em>','Follow real configuration, callback and outcome code, then use the feature map for later lessons.',body+actions(('/architecture.html','← UML with code at every step'),('/','Run the experiments →')))
readme='# Claude Agent SDK · Lesson 09 · The options object\n\nBased on Lesson09_The_Options_Object.pptx. A TypeScript lab that composes options, summarizes classroom TODOs, proves that pre-approval is not tool restriction, tests a programmatic Edit block against a project allow, and preserves a one-turn limit outcome.\n\n## What you will learn\n\n'+'\n'.join('- '+t+': '+d for t,d in learn)
readme+='\n\n## Configure and run\n\nUse Node.js 24+, npm and your own Anthropic key with access to the configured model. Python is not required to run this app.\n\n```powershell\ngit clone https://github.com/luiscoco/Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson09-app.git\ncd .\\Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson09-app\nnpm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env\nnpm start\n```\n\nFrom presentations, use `cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson09-options` instead of cloning. Open http://127.0.0.1:3109 and keep the terminal running. Ctrl+C stops it.\n\n## Create your .env file\n\nPreserve an existing .env. Copy the safe example if needed, enter the key locally and restart. The npm start and sample:env scripts load .env explicitly; shell variables take precedence.\n\n```dotenv\n'+env+'\n```\n\nOn Windows, if required, add `CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH=C:/Program Files/Git/bin/bash.exe` after confirming the installed path. Keep optional npm dependencies enabled. A second start recognizes this application; change PORT for another listener.\n\n## Run the experiments\n\n1. Keep Read-only TODO summary, maxTurns 8, SDK threshold $0.30 and low effort. Confirm the three TODO identifiers and unchanged status.txt.\n2. Choose Only Read pre-approved · Edit available. Observe Edit in system/init, the real callback allow decision and the actual file changing to reviewed.\n3. Choose Project allows Edit · options block it. Compare ["project"], the project allow file, disallowedTools and Edit missing from init. Confirm status.txt is unchanged.\n4. Return to TODO summary with maxTurns 1. Inspect error_max_turns and any preserved post-result exception notice. A tool request alone is not a completed summary.\n5. Download actual observations if useful. Run browser and CLI experiments sequentially.\n\n```powershell\nnpm run sample:env -- summary 8\nnpm run sample:env -- approval 8\nnpm run sample:env -- blocked 8\nnpm run sample:env -- summary 1\n```\n\n`sample` uses only the inherited shell environment. Each run resets its own private classroom files; no arbitrary user project path is accepted.\n\n## How the app was built\n\n'
for s in steps:readme+=f'### {s["number"]}. {s["title"]}\n\n{s["explanation"]}\n\nSource: `{s["source"]}`, lines {s["firstLine"]}–{s["lastLine"]}. Selected source; surrounding code omitted.\n\n```{s["language"]}\n{s["code"]}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## Interpret the evidence\n\n- tools configures availability; allowedTools pre-approves calls. In the controlled approval scenario Edit is available but not pre-approved. The real callback automatically approves only Edit on status.txt. No human approval dialog is simulated.\n- The blocked experiment loads a real project allow rule and programmatically disallows Edit. The actual init tools and unchanged file verify this specific interaction. It does not test managed policy or every settings-precedence combination. Permission deny rules have their own evaluation flow.\n- TypeScript env replaces the subprocess environment. The host spreads process.env before adding a private config home and a harmless classroom variable; only a safe projection is shown. The model is not asked to read environment variables.\n- maxTurns is a runtime turn limit, not an SDK message count. maxBudgetUsd is an estimate threshold, not an exact invoice or wall-clock guarantee. Effort is an independent configuration choice. The host also applies a timeout.\n- Typed error results are preserved if iteration subsequently throws. The actual file is read in finally, independently of the assistant summary. Provider failures are not replaced with stored answers.\n- Fixed directories and path hooks are local application guards, not an operating-system sandbox. No shell tool is available.\n- The feature map covers reference topics such as MCP, subagents, skills, structured output, persistence and sandboxing; those integrations are not run here. Python snippets are reference-only.\n- Sampling controls such as temperature, top_p and max_tokens belong to the Messages API, not this SDK options object. Use the Client SDK directly for that interface.\n\n## Maintenance\n\n```powershell\nnpm test\nnpm run build:client\npython scripts/build-pages.py\n```\n\nPython is optional for regenerating the documentation. All five student pages, coloured source snippets, local Markdown parser/sanitizer, mascot, UML, fixtures and application sources are bundled. .env, dependencies, runtime files, teaching-material, presentation/output/reviewed/v3 folders, videos, audio and PowerPoint remain excluded from Git.\n\n## References\n\n- [Configure the Agent SDK](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/configuration)\n- [Permission evaluation](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/permissions)\n- [Approval callbacks](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/user-input)\n- [TypeScript SDK reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/typescript)\n'
(APP/'README.md').write_text(readme,encoding='utf-8')
print('Built five Lesson 09 student pages, 13 source-linked UML steps, a feature map and README.')
